# vitest coverage report (WEB13 test:coverage writes it; the floor is the artifact, not the HTML)
#
# WEB17 (b) — DELIBERATELY NOT PUBLISHED, and this line is the record so the
# question is not re-opened by the next person who notices 184 untracked files.
# The number CI enforces is the statements floor in the `test:coverage` script,
# and a red floor prints its own numbers in the log; the HTML only answers WHICH
# LINES, which you get faster by running `npm run test:coverage` locally than by
# downloading an artifact. Contrast the Playwright report, which IS uploaded (on
# failure only): a browser failure is not reproducible from the log, so its
# artifact buys something this one does not. Publishing this would mean a Pages
# surface or a badge — a new outward-facing render, with a classification to
# decide, that nothing currently consumes.
coverage
